  "raw_response": "def solve(grid):\n    \"\"\"\n    Remove isolated non\u2011zero cells.\n    A cell is considered isolated if none of its eight neighbours\n    (including diagonals) contains a non\u2011zero value in the original grid.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not grid:\n        return grid\n\n    rows = len(grid)\n    cols = len(grid[0])\n\n    # Keep a copy of the original grid for neighbour checks\n    original = [row[:] for row in grid]\n\n    # Start with a copy of the original; we will zero out isolated cells\n    result = [row[:] for row in grid]\n\n    for i in range(rows):\n        for j in range(cols):\n            if original[i][j] == 0:\n                continue\n\n            # Check all eight neighbours\n            isolated = True\n            for di in (-1, 0, 1):\n                for dj in (-1, 0, 1):\n                    if di == 0 and dj == 0:\n                        continue\n                    ni, nj = i + di, j + dj\n                    if 0 <= ni < rows and 0 <= nj < cols:\n                        if original[ni][nj] != 0:\n                            isolated = False\n                            break\n                if not isolated:\n                    break\n\n            if isolated:\n                result[i][j] = 0\n\n    return result",
